// Failure golden: deriving K (equivalently UIP) MUST fail elaboration with a
// without-k diagnostic (ADR-76; the binding adequacy witness of the without-K
// discipline). An elaborator that accepts this program has implemented K.
//
// The program is the UIP statement over a diagonal identity type: matching
// `p : Path(Integer, n, n)` (and then `q`) against `here` requires solving the
// reflexive equation `n = n` by DELETION -- exactly the unification step
// without-k forbids (Cockx-Devriese-Piessens; the rung-2 lhs engine must
// decline that step itself, with this same diagnostic spelling). At rung 1
// here patterns do not exist at all, and `case` on an identity type is
// rejected with the without-k reservation -- so this witness fails today and
// stays a valid failure verbatim at rung 2.
//
// (Pathological tree: testing artifact, not pedagogy -- ADR-52 Decision C.)

def uip(n: Integer, p: Path(Integer, n, n), q: Path(Integer, n, n)) -> F(Path(Path(Integer, n, n), p, q)) {
  case p { here => case q { here => ret here(p) } }
}

//@ expect-diagnostic: without-k
//@ expect-diagnostics-all: without-k
